       "text": "I entered the order as written: ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily (6400 mg/day). The order ID is ORD-0001.\n\nThe order carries an override note. It says the dose is twice the usual maximum per dose and per day, that you confirmed it after the warning, and that no clinical reason was given. The note also recommends pharmacist review before dispensing, so pharmacy will probably contact you.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for this dose, I'd suggest adding it to the record. If you'd like a plan to watch for side effects, the usual checks are:\n- **Kidney function and electrolytes:** creatinine/BUN and potassium.\n- **Bleeding:** signs of GI bleeding, with hemoglobin checks.\n- **GI protection:** think about adding a proton pump inhibitor (PPI).\n\nI can enter any of these, or change the order, if you want."
